  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe probe op's protected-move law judged only the stylus ball (`probe_op::stylus_hits`). The stylus stem above the ball and the probe body were never checked. So a deep edge or corner touch beside a taller wall, or a touch under an overhang, could pass while the stem or body met the part.\n\n- `probe_op::stylus_cutter(tool)` describes the probe as a stack the cutters' solid law can read. The ball is the cutting atom. The stem is the shank band at the ball's radius, up to the stylus length. The body and any holder form one band at the wider radius.\n- `probe_op::stylus_reach_hits` runs the existing `verify::solid_hits` over every move, through its public seam with no copy. A stem or body meeting the part is a `ShankHit { part: true }`, and a rapid meeting it is `RapidInStock`. Both block the post. Only the ball may touch, so the expected contact excuses nothing above it, and a move the ball check already convicted isn't reported twice. The allowance is the existing `STYLUS_SLACK` (0.01 mm), so a stem riding tangent to the wall it touches stays clean.\n- `generate_probe` adds these warnings to the ball check's.\n\nDecisions are recorded in `docs/decisions/172-probe-shank-sweep.md`. No new warning kind: `ShankHit` is reused, because a new variant would change the project file format.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `Tool` has no stylus-diameter field, so the stem is modelled at the ball's radius. Real stems are thinner, so this can only over-report, never miss a hit. Body and holder share one band at the wider radius, which is also conservative.\n- No clean-bore fixture: the shape primitives can't build a block with a hole. The faceted-bore tangent maths matches the ball check, which already passes there.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/probe_reach.rs`, new suite)\n\n- `a_stem_that_meets_an_overhang_is_a_shank_hit`\n- `a_body_that_meets_a_tall_wall_is_a_shank_hit`\n- `clean_touches_stay_clean_under_the_reach_law`\n- `the_stylus_stack_is_ball_then_stem_then_body`\n- `a_short_stylus_deep_on_the_stock_edge_is_refused_by_the_op`\n\nThe existing `probe_op` suite passes 11/11. Gate: `scripts/gate.sh quick` (macOS) is green. clippy `-p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings` is clean.\n\nChangelog: Probe op: the stylus stem and the probe body are judged against the part on every probe move; a touch whose ball clears but whose stem or body meets a wall is refused as a shank hit (#172)\n\nFixes #172\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
